Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: close post-merge mutant survivors of #2173
 and #2214

Test-only. Post-merge check t_01a1d59498c0a89a found clauses that survived
exact-anchor mutants. Production behaviour is unchanged; these tests pin it.
Card t_01a1d5ada30e3458.

tests/gateway/test_update_requeue_stop_latches.py (#2173,
gateway/session_update_pause.py `_stopped_after_requeue`):
- A shutdown Stop (`stop_authority_turns`) that arrives while the requeue
  write runs finds the turn returned with no adopted agent and latches the
  generation in `pending_stops`. The head is cancelled and the latch must go
  with it. Kills A4 (drop the pending_stops / pending_stop_causes pops).
- A Stop latched during the requeue write cancels a head carrying retained
  native media; the media must be released with it. Kills A7 (drop
  `release_admission_media`).
- A3 alone (drop `update_stops.discard(admission_id)` in
  `_stopped_after_requeue`) is equivalent on every reachable path, so no test
  targets it. `park_or_interrupt` records the claim in `update_claims`
  (`remember_claim`) under the claim gate and mutation lock it holds through
  the requeue. So `requeue_unstarted`'s `update_claims.pop` always returns
  this admission and discards its latch, with no await before
  `_stopped_after_requeue`. The execution-stamp lookup in `interrupt_update`
  (claim missing from `update_claims`) never latches a Stop in that window.

tests/hermes_state/test_schema_init_memo_heal_retry.py (#2214):
- A memo-hit heal whose NULL-active UPDATE meets a lock is retried after
  HEAL_RETRY_S (30 s), not HEAL_INTERVAL_S. Kills B12
  (`_heal_null_active_rows` returns True on OperationalError).
- The full init keeps the delegate-marker heal's failure when the
  NULL-active heal after it succeeds, with no earlier interval claim. Kills
  B13 (`healed = self._heal_null_active_rows(cursor)`). (B13 was already
  killed on main by
  test_a_full_init_heal_failure_overrides_an_earlier_keys_interval_claim;
  this covers it without the earlier claim.)
- fail -> succeed -> fail warns twice. Kills B14 (a success not clearing
  `_heal_failing`).

Proof (sdlc-review scripts/mutants.py, scripts/run_tests.sh per file, base
b3745e62d5). Predictions were written before the runs and matched:
- new gateway file: A4 killed, A7 killed, A3-alone SURVIVED (equivalent)
- old test_update_requeue_stop_race.py: A4, A7, A3 SURVIVED
- new hermes_state file: B12 killed (2 tests), B13 killed, B14 killed
- old test_schema_init_memo_heals.py: B12 SURVIVED, B13 killed, B14 SURVIVED
- GREEN: 4 files, 13 tests passed, 0 failed (3 runs);
  scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok
